<title>USA: Computer Sciences gets 5-yr defense pact.</title>
<headline>Computer Sciences gets 5-yr defense pact.</headline>
<dateline>FALLS CHURCH, Va. 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Computer Sciences Corp said Thursday it had received a $113 million, five-year contract to provide technical support services to the Defense Department's accounting unit.</p>
<p>Computer Sciences will provide hardware migration and installation, systems modernization, maintenance, technology, documentation, training and project management.</p>
<p>The work will be done by its Integrated Systems division.</p>
<p>The contract has a base value of $24 million and a cumulative value of $113 million, if all options are exercised over a five-year period, it said.</p>
